# Open Gaming License — Notice for WAYFARER (Working Draft)

WAYFARER Core Rules (c) 2026 by the Wayfarer design team.

## System Reference Document (SRD) Scope
The following game mechanics are released as the WAYFARER SRD under the
Open Gaming License v1.0a, free for others to use, adapt, and republish in
their own products:

- The Pair Roll resolution mechanic (Facet die + Craft die vs. Target Number)
- Target Number tiers (5/7/9/11) and step-based modifier system
- Critical (max-max / double-6) and Fumble (double-1) rules with Boons and Turnbacks
- The Tear condition track (0–5 steady, 6–9 battered, 10 gone)
- Verve resource and its listed uses
- Disciplines, Callings template, Marks advancement scheme
- Journey daily cycle (March / Wayfinding / Encampment), Terrain Levels 1–5,
  weather and party modifiers
- Rites, Pillars, casting costs, Dissonance table
- Combat sequence, called shots, Evasion, damage formula, Price/Fear negotiation rule
- Hope token economy and published award triggers

## Product Identity (NOT open)
The following remain the property of the creators and may not be reused:
- The name "WAYFARER" and its logo/branding
- The setting name "Cairnreach" and all proper nouns (Kirksteel, Sunwood,
  River-glass, named Rites, named Callings text/flavor)
- All original artwork, layout, and example text

Full OGL v1.0a text to be appended before publication (standard Wizards of
the Coast boilerplate, unmodified).